# WHAT THIS IMAGE DEPENDS ON. The image installs requirements.txt, the lock
# made from this file (every package pinned, with hashes):
#     python3 scripts/image_locks.py lock instagram
# Edit here, then re-lock; never edit requirements.txt by hand.
#
# instagram's OWN dependencies, installed only into this Actor's image.
#
# PLAYWRIGHT IS MANDATORY HERE, unlike the facebook Actor. That one's page and
# group paths are browser-free by design, so its image carries no Chromium at
# all. This collector's engine opens `sync_playwright()` in EVERY entry point:
# the HTTP replay tier is Tier 1 for the data, but the tokens it replays with
# (x-ig-app-id, x-ig-www-claim, the exact user-agent) are captured from a real
# page load first. There is no browser-free path to them, so the image is ~1.3GB
# rather than ~180MB. Verified by reading the engine, not assumed.
# MUST EQUAL THE BASE IMAGE'S TAG (Dockerfile FROM playwright/python:vX).
# The image ships the browsers for ITS version only; a different package
# version looks for a browser build that is not there and every launch fails
# ("Executable doesn't exist at /ms-playwright/..."). test_actor_images.py
# checks the two agree, so a base-image bump fails CI until this follows.
playwright==1.64.1

# The HTTP replay tier. h2 comes with the [http2] extra, which it prefers.
httpx[http2]==0.28.1

# The analysis and report stage -- the vendored processors/ai/reports layer's
# own dependencies, scanned from its imports:
#
#   anthropic        ai/claude.py and ai/segmentation.py
#   reportlab        reports/instagram_report.py (the PDF)
#   python-dotenv    config.py, which ai/claude.py imports for the API key
#   arabic-reshaper  \ reports/instagram_report.py shapes Arabic text for the
#   python-bidi      / PDF, and real accounts here post in Arabic
#
# reports/dashboard.py writes HTML with the standard library only.
anthropic>=0.40
reportlab>=4.0
python-dotenv>=1.0
arabic-reshaper>=3.0
python-bidi>=0.4
